<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Felice Baciocchi</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1762">1762</a>–<a href="/years/1841">1841</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Felice Baciocchi was a Corsican army officer who married <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>'s sister <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elisa-bonaparte">Elisa Bonaparte</a> in 1797. In 1805 Napoleon made the couple Princes of Lucca and Piombino, but Elisa held real power and Felice mostly commanded troops. When Elisa became Grand Duchess of Tuscany in 1809 he served as military commander there. After 1814 he lived quietly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bologna">Bologna</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/felice-baciocchi.jpg" alt="Felice Baciocchi" width="320" height="432" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pietro Benvenuti · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Felice_Baciocchi_Bonaparte.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
